Give the section of concept-files.tex its own label.
\DefineSection{OpenAndClosedStreams} is used both for Section 20.1.2
(File Operations on Open and Closed Streams) and for Section 21.1.1.1.2
(Open and Closed Streams); the second silently replaced the first, so the
two references in dict-files.tex that mean the file operations pointed at
the stream section.  The 20.1.2 section is now OpenAndClosedStreamsFiles,
and dict-files.tex (lines 68 and 152, in the same position) names it.
setup-sections.tex, the table the label commands read, gets the same
rename on line 257 (the glossary's references keep line 261).
The glossary's two references keep the stream section.
--- concept-files.tex
+++ concept-files.tex
@@ -47,1 +47,1 @@
-\DefineSection{OpenAndClosedStreams}
+\DefineSection{OpenAndClosedStreamsFiles}
--- dict-files.tex
+++ dict-files.tex
@@ -68,1 +68,1 @@
-{\secref\OpenAndClosedStreams},
+{\secref\OpenAndClosedStreamsFiles},
@@ -152,1 +152,1 @@
-{\secref\OpenAndClosedStreams},
+{\secref\OpenAndClosedStreamsFiles},
--- setup-sections.tex
+++ setup-sections.tex
@@ -257,1 +257,1 @@
-\def\OpenAndClosedStreams{Section 20.1.2 (File Operations on Open and Closed Streams)}%
+\def\OpenAndClosedStreamsFiles{Section 20.1.2 (File Operations on Open and Closed Streams)}%
